estion/math-academy-id "q-118581" :question/problem "Given that $y=y(t),$ what is the carrying capacity of the following logistic growth model?\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=720y-8{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=5\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nA diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's factor the right-hand side of the given equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=8y(90-y),\\,y(0)=5.\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=90.$ Therefore, the carrying capacity is $90.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118581/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91856ca3-4d9c-51c4-910b-27acba52156e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118581"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-118580/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "e0d2a12c-ff7f-5492-a87e-500b1c5c5f13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118580/selection/478fd1e25e3e34a29fea1c3ec66147c061ba20da2ebcc365831518058573cd79" :answer/id #uuid "21616dae-175d-522a-ae8f-d9105f739576" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118580/selection/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" :answer/id #uuid "71b31ba4-a582-539c-ab8e-04a486ea9ad4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118580/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "dc8198b8-8fed-5396-b221-276f40685a24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ens