mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's factor the right-hand side of the given equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3y(400-y),\\,y(0)=50.\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=400.$ Therefore, the carrying capacity is $400.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118577/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91856ca3-4d9c-51c4-910b-27acba52156e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118577"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-118560/selection/e12f73422a456eca8c83cae70999c506825a539631c33c529fb793c051a91c96" :answer/id #uuid "a08c37d3-d2b1-5b55-a954-6a6de82990a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "450" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118560/selection/46f5cf111c64bb246ccb0222ffdb16d4820c33f4fcd20606431b1cc8617909f1" :answer/id #uuid "b47c5ce0-9a74-576f-9efe-be9d4e39d0ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118560/selection/c5b7aea79f73ebc562cbcff24725697bdc076b45efa2d86abecbb1b4fa682579" :answer/id #uuid "371fb11b-71b8-5a8e-97c7-0947148e88e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118560/selection/a4f28cb7bb757488a58afe90ebae3aa4fedc3e05d8d3c20faaf2869176d717ef" :answer/id #uuid "93dd6090-2cf2-536f-be00-96efad2df185" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,250" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118560/selection/feccf1d787deaa2db8d6f1c5144663a62c7f847db88780db80f98a131046d01c" :answer/id #uuid "cdb553d4-f9da-541f-a03d-0f5234ec801d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "250" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118560/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "66650271-56a9-502c-ab02-30c18494437c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-118560/selection/46f5cf111c64bb246ccb0222ffdb16d4820c33f4fcd20606431b1cc8617909f1" :answer-field/choices ["q-118560/selection/e12f73422a456eca8c83cae70999c506825a539631c33c529fb793c051a91c96" "q-118560/selection/46f5cf111c64bb246ccb0222ffdb16d4820c33f4fcd20606431b1cc8617909f1" "q-118560/selection/c5b7aea79f73ebc562cbcff24725697bdc076b45efa2d86abecbb1b4fa682579" "q-118560/selection/a4f28cb7bb757488a58afe90ebae3aa4fedc3e05d8d3c20faaf2869176d717ef" "q-118560/selection/feccf1d787deaa2db8d6f1c5144663a62c7f847db88780db80f98a131046d01c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118560" :question/id #uuid "a67cb8d5-18ca-5d11-9dfc-d7a49d4d64b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-118560" :question/problem "The population $y(t)$ of mockingbirds in a forest follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=0.6y-0.0003{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=250,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in months, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible population of mockingbirds?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =0.6y-0.0003{y}^{2} \\\\  & =0.0003y(2\\,000-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=2\\,000.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $2\\,000,$ and we conclude that the number of mockingbirds cannot exceed $2\\,000.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-118560/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4728b3c6-a600-569d-922e-228e9f6fb2a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118560"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-118561/selection/bf9a21fe4dc212a46e36120707112677355d58d140bf05555ecb2406d2818099" :answer/id #uuid "2927dd01-798a-53f5-a985-8571f8326f77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118561/selection/e4e5059e43747775ab94d8b29ebd4ed8575e1523e102644a8c50e6df8642fce9" :answer/id #uuid "7841e048-06f5-53ad-b250-a5548e9ccc58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "550" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118561/selection/c5b7aea79f73ebc562cbcff24725697bdc076b45efa2d86abecbb1b4fa682579" :answer/id #uuid "c0fc8f5b-f532-55fb-9ae1-3c7aa41ab472" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118561/selection/3f36e2551412bcd246b99585827478f762e970eb94cf09ec8ccb07367bcc6c38" :answer/id #uuid "e46c55d3-1ccc-5291-99d2-151a4328b914" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "465" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118561/selection/176ce96a130f432c9d77726b4cdaccf1ca6ddba8dd0e5e3773d86d5d0aea4a18" :answer/id #uuid "ef0cc530-300e-545a-a4e3-14be21f35cc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "800" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118561/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6122d29a-ea43-57b8-abea-622b420c9fa5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-118561/selection/c5b7aea79f73ebc562cbcff24725697bdc076b45efa2d86abecbb1b4fa682579" :answer-field/choices ["q-118561/selection/bf9a21fe4dc212a46e36120707112677355d58d140bf05555ecb2406d2818099" "q-118561/selection/e4e5059e43747775ab94d8b29ebd4ed8575e1523e102644a8c50e6df8642fce9" "q-118561/selection/c5b7aea79f73ebc562cbcff24725697bdc076b45efa2d86abecbb1b4fa682579" "q-118561/selection/3f36e2551412bcd246b99585827478f762e970eb94cf09ec8ccb07367bcc6c38" "q-118561/selection/176ce96a130f432c9d77726b4cdaccf1ca6ddba8dd0e5e3773d86d5d0aea4a18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118561" :question/id #uuid "fbe1958e-67bc-532f-b098-5d3f40081ea7" :question/math-academy-id "q-118561" :question/problem "The population $y(t)$ of sloths in a forest follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=0.3y(2-\\frac{y}{300}),\\,y(0)=135,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible sloth population?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =0.3y(2-\\frac{y}{300}) \\\\  & =0.3y(\\frac{600-y}{300}) \\\\  & =\\frac{0.3y}{300}(600-y) \\\\  & =0.001y(600-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=600.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $600,$ and we conclude that the number of sloths cannot exceed $600.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118561/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4728b3c6-a600-569d-922e-228e9f6fb2a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118561"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353477/field-1/feccf1d787deaa2db8d6f1c5144663a62c7f847db88780db80f98a131046d01c" :answer/id #uuid "703cc21e-264b-5fe7-9742-04ed82869b48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "250" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353477/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4938831-5227-5c39-9a6e-258e3e610976" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353477/field-1/feccf1d787deaa2db8d6f1c5144663a62c7f847db88780db80f98a131046d01c" :answer-field/choices ["q-353477/field-1/feccf1d787deaa2db8d6f1c5144663a62c7f847db88780db80f98a131046d01c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353477" :question/id #uuid "05786f4e-51a8-5af3-98a4-43cb1a4556c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-353477" :question/problem "The number $y(t)$ of people who have participated in a viral trend on social media follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=1250y-5{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=40,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in hours, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible number of participants?\n\nThe maximum possible number of participants is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible number of participants in the trend. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/d8133f1c4203903bac606bbae61c73717e2ba2dc15a97a77f48eaaeaf4736d06.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =1250y-5{y}^{2} \\\\  & =5y(250-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=250.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $250,$ and we conclude that the maximum possible number of participants is $250.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353477/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4728b3c6-a600-569d-922e-228e9f6fb2a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353477"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119849/selection/9ff8157b20b64a245202d0cf913e4397546006c7c38b2b70bb634b860aa35720" :answer/id #uuid "23463754-4a4e-500c-8d99-48fc6c65db94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "400" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119849/selection/9b10e4fe42e7be5844ebc6179cc206bead6386e5fe2e577e96c32eb2db497c1c" :answer/id #uuid "5fc6becc-58aa-5688-9495-64431dbc583f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,720" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119849/selection/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18" :answer/id #uuid "3ba24c1b-3b4f-5a64-ab6a-d848e14d6558" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "180" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119849/selection/8a327e90361335c9d8ac8453020348227e5edbbf6b0ae2e2ea6e03ef50bc3f4c" :answer/id #uuid "666d246f-9b65-53bb-b49b-91b6150237e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,300" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119849/selection/9b7cb08b5fba1520882af22c5e9056849bdc3ec89fb2c112694533c83d338edd" :answer/id #uuid "3e746939-8de3-5229-9ce2-722df8dc8c3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119849/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e1015a5-8c4c-5a55-8e9b-9a782dc93cdb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119849/selection/8a327e90361335c9d8ac8453020348227e5edbbf6b0ae2e2ea6e03ef50bc3f4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-119849/selection/9ff8157b20b64a245202d0cf913e4397546006c7c38b2b70bb634b860aa35720" "q-119849/selection/9b10e4fe42e7be5844ebc6179cc206bead6386e5fe2e577e96c32eb2db497c1c" "q-119849/selection/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18" "q-119849/selection/8a327e90361335c9d8ac8453020348227e5edbbf6b0ae2e2ea6e03ef50bc3f4c" "q-119849/selection/9b7cb08b5fba1520882af22c5e9056849bdc3ec89fb2c112694533c83d338edd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119849" :question/id #uuid "b4a41fa6-e7d1-54e2-a912-d65af3313e72" :question/math-academy-id "q-119849" :question/problem "The population $y(t)$ of giraffes on a certain African wildlife reserve follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=17.2y-0.004{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=180,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible population of giraffes?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =17.2y-0.004{y}^{2} \\\\  & =0.004y(4\\,300-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=4\\,300.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $4\\,300,$ and we conclude that the number of giraffes cannot exceed $4\\,300.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119849/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4728b3c6-a600-569d-922e-228e9f6fb2a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119849"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119846/selection/2341d4beafc19cb7b8396e0b9f21c544ec7f6a786fc846e9361e36afd0b43437" :answer/id #uuid "ea6513c8-a6f1-53df-81ac-d55079bb4e31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "43" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119846/selection/0086db6077a62a5e2d9c771f7cdf57bea92b1de496b4d9b1d9c50dc1e5b58991" :answer/id #uuid "801df426-3e35-5c86-b8da-7a5d85a0b3c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119846/selection/9ff8157b20b64a245202d0cf913e4397546006c7c38b2b70bb634b860aa35720" :answer/id #uuid "6297c3b2-7f6b-53ea-8e1a-b8eb96ca74b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "400" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119846/selection/f1a3f6364b4b6488166c92c743a5a8e2e2bdb28aff5bc6025ac2678cb4926932" :answer/id #uuid "b763f903-a7c1-5028-999b-000e7761709c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "200" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119846/selection/bf6afcfe4ab7cf808a438174458e9ee42216202dbe1a5ae3c8a51b18bafe5be1" :answer/id #uuid "3f21711b-302e-562a-b710-4bcd13d7fd28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,400" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119846/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "58556f93-669f-513a-826a-f8a45ba03e1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119846/selection/bf6afcfe4ab7cf808a438174458e9ee42216202dbe1a5ae3c8a51b18bafe5be1" :answer-field/choices ["q-119846/selection/2341d4beafc19cb7b8396e0b9f21c544ec7f6a786fc846e9361e36afd0b43437" "q-119846/selection/0086db6077a62a5e2d9c771f7cdf57bea92b1de496b4d9b1d9c50dc1e5b58991" "q-119846/selection/9ff8157b20b64a245202d0cf913e4397546006c7c38b2b70bb634b860aa35720" "q-119846/selection/f1a3f6364b4b6488166c92c743a5a8e2e2bdb28aff5bc6025ac2678cb4926932" "q-119846/selection/bf6afcfe4ab7cf808a438174458e9ee42216202dbe1a5ae3c8a51b18bafe5be1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119846" :question/id #uuid "18201405-cccb-5540-8a05-32c9fb70b5f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-119846" :question/problem "The population $y(t)$ of dolphins in a certain ocean follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4y(7-\\frac{y}{200}),\\,y(0)=43,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible dolphin population?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =4y(7-\\frac{y}{200}) \\\\  & =4y(\\frac{1\\,400-y}{200}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{200}y(1\\,400-y) \\\\  & =0.02y(1\\,400-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=1\\,400.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $1\\,400,$ and we conclude that the number of dolphins cannot exceed $1\\,400.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-119846/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4728b3c6-a600-569d-922e-228e9f6fb2a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119846"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-51379/selection/46f5cf111c64bb246ccb0222ffdb16d4820c33f4fcd20606431b1cc8617909f1" :answer/id #uuid "74d5a8e1-d619-5d13-b65c-f798c83b281f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51379/selection/bf9a21fe4dc212a46e36120707112677355d58d140bf05555ecb2406d2818099" :answer/id #uuid "c92f64a5-3f74-513f-9bf4-ba82c1aabd1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51379/selection/bf6afcfe4ab7cf808a438174458e9ee42216202dbe1a5ae3c8a51b18bafe5be1" :answer/id #uuid "f5d22db2-72f9-56eb-9446-d2100f6dc045" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,400" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51379/selection/478fd1e25e3e34a29fea1c3ec66147c061ba20da2ebcc365831518058573cd79" :answer/id #uuid "975874bc-9c40-5357-bdba-aa5a5e586006" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51379/selection/176ce96a130f432c9d77726b4cdaccf1ca6ddba8dd0e5e3773d86d5d0aea4a18" :answer/id #uuid "e61da589-105c-59a6-9661-47862746b2fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "800" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51379/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ab70a64-3f86-508c-87a1-91dc20713acb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-51379/selection/bf9a21fe4dc212a46e36120707112677355d58d140bf05555ecb2406d2818099" :answer-field/choices ["q-51379/selection/46f5cf111c64bb246ccb0222ffdb16d4820c33f4fcd20606431b1cc8617909f1" "q-51379/selection/bf9a21fe4dc212a46e36120707112677355d58d140bf05555ecb2406d2818099" "q-51379/selection/bf6afcfe4ab7cf808a438174458e9ee42216202dbe1a5ae3c8a51b18bafe5be1" "q-51379/selection/478fd1e25e3e34a29fea1c3ec66147c061ba20da2ebcc365831518058573cd79" "q-51379/selection/176ce96a130f432c9d77726b4cdaccf1ca6ddba8dd0e5e3773d86d5d0aea4a18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-51379" :question/id #uuid "230cd702-7176-5194-8d85-6e3150ad5869" :question/math-academy-id "q-51379" :question/problem "The population $P(t)$of rabbits in a particular forest follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=4P-0.002{P}^{2},\\,P(0)=100,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the rabbit population growing at the fastest possible rate?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/9d8f5340bba4d3c407e43f2bc64a4aa2ea986be89b8024baaa4e8ae65e96e5d5.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =4P-0.002{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.002P(2\\,000-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=2\\,000.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $2\\,000,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\,000=1\\,000.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-51379/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7293561d-2ddf-581d-b086-9754fdb2ff16"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51379"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83974/selection/feccf1d787deaa2db8d6f1c5144663a62c7f847db88780db80f98a131046d01c" :answer/id #uuid "dc980a47-3b1c-5500-9042-eec79ce09a63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "250" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83974/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer/id #uuid "c846fd60-9bc4-5d94-ae81-1daa1676e579" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83974/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" :answer/id #uuid "09e51317-34e6-56f7-85a0-e0f09f18514d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83974/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "56e8c70c-2d6e-5ce1-8338-20595e8fa9e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83974/selection/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64" :answer/id #uuid "8073da54-1255-593e-8d23-d7b8c859823a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83974/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1dc722d6-491f-559f-bbfd-dcb7c8b4e873" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83974/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer-field/choices ["q-83974/selection/feccf1d787deaa2db8d6f1c5144663a62c7f847db88780db80f98a131046d01c" "q-83974/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" "q-83974/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" "q-83974/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-83974/selection/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83974" :question/id #uuid "7032cb07-ee0e-5cbc-b7e2-ff14cc27887a" :question/math-academy-id "q-83974" :question/problem "The population $P(t)$ of catfishes in a particular lake follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.1P-0.002{P}^{2},\\,P(0)=5,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the catfish population growing at the fastest possible rate?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/9d8f5340bba4d3c407e43f2bc64a4aa2ea986be89b8024baaa4e8ae65e96e5d5.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.1P-0.002{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.002P(50-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=50.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $50,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 50=25.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83974/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7293561d-2ddf-581d-b086-9754fdb2ff16"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83974"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353487/field-1/ffbc744ca20ef36377a3441056a67f0392c44aacee8af37883958fa626c1b473" :answer/id #uuid "d9c46616-1d43-5fe5-8d11-9c61cb7c40e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1200" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353487/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "78bba66e-2745-50e7-996c-e592a67d174a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353487/field-1/ffbc744ca20ef36377a3441056a67f0392c44aacee8af37883958fa626c1b473" :answer-field/choices ["q-353487/field-1/ffbc744ca20ef36377a3441056a67f0392c44aacee8af37883958fa626c1b473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353487" :question/id #uuid "38a73021-b915-534e-9dcf-7cdc220a2098" :question/math-academy-id "q-353487" :question/problem "The number $P(t)$ of potential buyers in a market for a new product follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=7200P-3{P}^{2},\\,P(0)=100,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the number of potential buyers growing at the fastest possible rate?\n\n$P=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/9019b26b417c757bbfab79afb39379c1fc7a892bc44e934c6f23c339deacfd68.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =7200P-3{P}^{2} \\\\  & =3P(2400-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=2400.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $2400,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2400=1200.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353487/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7293561d-2ddf-581d-b086-9754fdb2ff16"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353487"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119855/selection/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64" :answer/id #uuid "2dfec2cd-b341-5ce0-9acf-0333667a2fff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119855/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "8797f27b-8233-5dbf-912c-84d80a18578a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119855/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" :answer/id #uuid "60df3e3e-7a2c-5e73-b841-efa6e14c0893" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119855/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "d76a52a1-f6f0-54f0-b455-e69b65909aa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119855/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer/id #uuid "dbcba33f-28a8-5425-bfb6-befb33a20137" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119855/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a33dc90-988c-53e7-a11e-45433f2ccbe3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119855/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer-field/choices ["q-119855/selection/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64" "q-119855/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-119855/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" "q-119855/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-119855/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119855" :question/id #uuid "3451059c-1c4e-54f9-9dc9-14e12f6043d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119855" :question/problem "The rate of growth in the number of turtles $P(t)$ that developed fungus on their shells in a certain aquarium follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.6P-0.012{P}^{2},\\,P(0)=2.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in months. For which value of $P$ is the number of turtles that developed fungus growing at the fastest possible rate?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/9d8f5340bba4d3c407e43f2bc64a4aa2ea986be89b8024baaa4e8ae65e96e5d5.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.6P-0.012{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.012P(50-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=50.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $50,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 50=25.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119855/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7293561d-2ddf-581d-b086-9754fdb2ff16"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119855"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348210/field-1/2ae91f4acef1e258303c5198524ee0c09d54456f734e655864530e0fc07a0a9d" :answer/id #uuid "cd8394bd-475c-5c84-b9d7-4bbc5985335d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "700" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348210/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2dd3e753-ef6b-56c9-a555-79e2d3aeec27" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348210/field-1/2ae91f4acef1e258303c5198524ee0c09d54456f734e655864530e0fc07a0a9d" :answer-field/choices ["q-348210/field-1/2ae91f4acef1e258303c5198524ee0c09d54456f734e655864530e0fc07a0a9d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348210" :question/id #uuid "b73643b4-813a-56d4-b435-03780ad9410a" :question/math-academy-id "q-348210" :question/problem "The population $P(t)$ of beavers in a certain river follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.0008P(1\\,400-P),\\,P(0)=60.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the beaver population growing at the fastest possible rate?\n\n$P=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/9019b26b417c757bbfab79afb39379c1fc7a892bc44e934c6f23c339deacfd68.png)\n\nFrom our equation, we see that $a=1400.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $1400,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1400=700.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-348210/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7293561d-2ddf-581d-b086-9754fdb2ff16"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348210"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9376"] :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation for the function $y = y(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\ny' = 2y\\left(60 - \\frac{y}{3} \\right), \\qquad y(0) = 10\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\displaystyle \\lim_{t\\to\\infty}{y(t)}?$" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\ny' = ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k > 0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a > y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nA diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2y(60-\\frac{y}{3}) \\\\  & =2y(\\frac{180-y}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{3}(180-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a = 180.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $180.$\n\nFor a given logistic growth model, $y\\to a$ as $t\\to\\infty.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim_{t\\to\\infty}{y(t)} = 180.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9375"] :question/problem "The population $y(t)$ of some foxes in a forest follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\ny' =0.5y - 0.002y^2, \\qquad y(0) = 25,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in months, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible fox population?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\ny' = ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k > 0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a > y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =0.5y-0.002{y}^{2} \\\\  & =0.002y(250-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a = 250.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $250,$ and we conclude that the number of foxes cannot exceed $250.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7324"] :question/problem "The rate of growth in the number of people $P(t)$ infected with a particular virus  follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d} P}{\\mathrm{d} t} =  4P - 0.000\\,01  P^2,  \\qquad P(0) = 5\\,000,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in days, since the virus outbreak began. For which value of $P$ is the number of people infected with the virus growing at the fastest possible rate?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\nP' = kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k > 0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a > P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P = \\dfrac12a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/9d8f5340bba4d3c407e43f2bc64a4aa2ea986be89b8024baaa4e8ae65e96e5d5.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =4P-0.000\\,01{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.000\\,01P(400\\,000-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a = 400\\,000.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $400\\,000,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP = \\dfrac12a = \\dfrac12\\cdot 400\\,000 = 200\\,000.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
